{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792495538,"nonce":"BeBa6LNNFRNFZBr5znWSXA5g6A8=","message":"All initial composite application regressions (six GPU cases plus one CPU fingerprint case) pass normally and with forced VB/DT capabilities; the existing four motion cases also pass in all three modes. Existing normal producer2, overlay7, aux2, display-list33 and fill-rule1 regressions pass. Temporary capability overrides were restored.\n\nAdditional source finding before finalization: the walker's promoted DynamicRegion was derived from bg_primitive_aabb, which does not include tessellated paths or nested layer-effect margins. Ordered baking alone would crop blur/shadow output at that region boundary. The footprint now reuses the same ordered node/bounds calculation as baking; the walker queries it for promoted CSS and motion regions. Open outer commands at region capture are balanced by the parser. A true path-only footprint test and an actual CSS-promoted nested blur-halo pixel case cover this addition. This is a source finding followed by positive regression, not a pre-fix pixel control. The native expansion convention is unchanged.\n\nFixture corrections during development: the first motion fixture accidentally placed base opacity on a single-child div inside the Motion wrapper; it was adjusted to test a nested multi-child group directly. Polygon clip vertices use the primitive-local frame, not screen coordinates. CPU footprint expectations now follow the existing native two-radius blur expansion rather than an assumed three-radius convention. No renderer changes were made for those fixture mistakes.","files":null}]}